<title>TURKEY: Istanbul gold prices rise, volume down.</title>
<headline>Istanbul gold prices rise, volume down.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Istanbul gold exchange prices rose on Friday as world markets steadied.</p>
<p>Values closed at $343.90 an ounce and 1,326,400 lira per gram from Thursday's $343.50 and 1,324,900, dealers said.</p>
<p>Volume fell sharply to 419 kilos  -- 349 kilos in lira terms and 70 in dollar terms -- from 855 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Turkish lira fell on Friday to 119,840 lira against the dollar from 119,750 at Thursday's close.</p>
<p>--Istanbul newsroom +90 212 275 0875</p>
</text>
